' The capitalist state: class model
' Companion notes: notes/state.md — full stereotype legend: notes/stereotypes.md
'
' The state is the public power of the capitalist class. Tax is a compulsory
' share of the product (mostly surplus value; sometimes a cut into the wage).
' Nationalisation changes who personifies capital; it does not abolish
' wage-labour or accumulation (Marx; SPGB).

@startuml state
title IX. The state — public power of capital, not a source of value
caption Tax is a share of the product; nationalisation is still capital: notes/state.md

hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<social relation>> #EDE7F6
  BackgroundColor<<historically specific>> #FFEBEE
  BackgroundColor<<personification>> #FFF8E1
  BackgroundColor<<abstract det.>> #E3F2FD
}

package "I. The relation the state belongs to" as P1 {
  class CapitalistModeOfProduction <<historically specific>> {
    wage-labour and capital
    (full definition: surplus-value-capital.puml)
  }
  class CapitalistClass <<historically specific>> {
    monopoly of the means of life
    (full definition: surplus-value-capital.puml)
  }
  class CapitalistState <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    public power of the capitalist class
    force, law, money, tax
    not a producer of value
  }
  class StateAsNeutralArbiter <<abstract det.>> {
    {abstract}
    rejected: the state stands
    above classes and creates
    fairness by policy
  }
}

package "II. Tax — a compulsory share" as P2 {
  class SurplusValue <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    unpaid labour
    (full definition: surplus-value-capital.puml)
  }
  class Wage <<historically specific>> {
    price of labour-power
    possible channel of the levy
    (full definition: surplus-value-capital.puml)
  }
  class Tax <<historically specific>> {
    compulsory deduction
    source is the product of labour
    mostly a cut of s; can stick in v
  }
  class TaxCreatesValue <<abstract det.>> {
    {abstract}
    rejected: the levy is a
    fourth source of value
    beside unpaid labour
  }
}

package "III. What the levy funds" as P3 {
  class ForceAndLaw <<historically specific>> {
    police, courts, military
    maintains the class order
  }
  class PublicInfrastructure <<historically specific>> {
    roads, ports, power
    cheapens conditions of production
    does not create s
  }
  class StateReproductionOfLP <<historically specific>> {
    schools, health, benefits
    enters reproduction of labour-power
  }
  class CentralBank <<historically specific>> {
    issues fiat
    (full definition: finance.puml)
  }
}

package "IV. Nationalisation" as P4 {
  class Capital <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    value that valorizes itself
    (full definition: surplus-value-capital.puml)
  }
  class StateCapital <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    capital whose legal owner
    is the state
    still M – C … P … C' – M'
    if it buys LP and sells
  }
  class StateBureaucracy <<personification>> {
    personification of state capital
    not abolition of the role
  }
  class NationalisationAbolishesCapital <<abstract det.>> {
    {abstract}
    rejected: public title deeds
    end wage-labour and accumulation
  }
}

CapitalistModeOfProduction *-- CapitalistClass
CapitalistModeOfProduction *-- CapitalistState
CapitalistClass --> CapitalistState : its public power
CapitalistState --> Tax : levies
Tax --> SurplusValue : mainly deducted from
Wage --> Tax : may channel
Tax --> Wage : can stick as a cut in
CapitalistState --> ForceAndLaw : funds
CapitalistState --> PublicInfrastructure : funds
CapitalistState --> StateReproductionOfLP : funds
CapitalistState --> CentralBank : backs
PublicInfrastructure --> SurplusValue : conditions of production\n(does not create s)
StateReproductionOfLP --> Wage : enters reproduction of
CapitalistState --> StateCapital : may own as
StateBureaucracy --> StateCapital : personifies
StateCapital --|> Capital
StateCapital --> SurplusValue : still appropriates\nif it exploits LP
StateAsNeutralArbiter ..> CapitalistState : mistakes a class power for
TaxCreatesValue ..> Tax : mistakes a share for a source
NationalisationAbolishesCapital ..> StateCapital : mistakes a change of title for

P1 -[hidden]right-> P2
P2 -[hidden]right-> P3
P3 -[hidden]right-> P4

note top of TaxCreatesValue
  **No fourth source of value**
  Interest, rent, and tax are claims
  on the product of labour. The state
  does not produce surplus value.
  Who writes the cheque is not
  the source: wages can be the conduit.
end note

note bottom of Tax
  If the value of labour-power holds,
  a wage-tax tends to be shifted onto s.
  If it sticks, real wages fall:
  a cut into necessary labour, still
  not a new creation of value.
end note

note bottom of StateCapital
  SPGB: state capitalism.
  Buying, selling, and employing
  wage-labour under a public seal
  is still capital. Accumulation
  continues if the unit competes.
end note

@enduml
